1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:15,206 --> 00:00:16,280
Are you really pregnant?

9
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,500
Yes, I am.

10
00:00:18,544 --> 00:00:20,620
Didn't you say you had a contraceptive implant?

11
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,160
But I'm not having an abortion.

12
00:00:22,286 --> 00:00:23,480
I'm keeping the baby.

13
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:27,600
That's the right decision. It's our baby, after all.

14
00:00:27,774 --> 00:00:29,640
I'll take you for your prenatal checkups.

15
00:00:29,955 --> 00:00:32,960
And these are vitamins and prenatal supplements.

16
00:00:33,304 --> 00:00:34,840
Just take them like you did during your last pregnancy.

17
00:00:35,102 --> 00:00:37,240
Mutta's pregnancy test results are back.

18
00:00:37,299 --> 00:00:38,894
- Say it.
- She's not pregnant!

19
00:00:39,715 --> 00:00:40,920
Ta, so you're not pregnant after all?

20
00:00:41,187 --> 00:00:43,640
And throw away those pills I gave you.

21
00:00:43,795 --> 00:00:45,560
I just wanted to test you, Director.

22
00:00:45,688 --> 00:00:47,640
Let me assure you

23
00:00:47,736 --> 00:00:48,737
that one day,

24
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,001
I'll divorce Napha and come live with you. I promise.

25
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:54,141
Okay, I'll wait.

26
00:00:54,541 --> 00:00:56,720
I had the pills Jenphop gave you checked.

27
00:00:57,142 --> 00:00:59,640
One was a painkiller, and the other was a sleeping pill.

28
00:00:59,712 --> 00:01:01,720
As for the suppository, it was an abortion drug.

29
00:01:04,302 --> 00:01:05,640
Ta?

30
00:01:07,603 --> 00:01:10,204
Why are you looking at me like that? Is something wrong?

31
00:01:14,211 --> 00:01:16,360
Where are you, Ta? What are you doing?

32
00:01:17,459 --> 00:01:19,507
I'm at a relative's house.

33
00:01:20,536 --> 00:01:21,840
I'll be going to bed soon.

34
00:01:22,366 --> 00:01:23,960
Don't forget to take the medicine I gave you.

35
00:01:24,387 --> 00:01:27,160
Oh, and I had a doctor friend order those suppositories from overseas.

36
00:01:27,368 --> 00:01:28,760
They were very expensive, Ta.

37
00:01:28,966 --> 00:01:30,320
They're to keep our baby healthy.

38
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:31,901
Okay.

39
00:01:32,587 --> 00:01:34,000
I'll use one tonight.

40
00:02:14,496 --> 00:02:15,560
Hello, Nin.

41
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:18,401
What time is your flight?

42
00:02:18,992 --> 00:02:22,040
Okay, see you tomorrow.

43
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:25,000
I bought tons of groceries to cook with.

44
00:02:26,870 --> 00:02:29,240
I'll just sleep on the sofa.

45
00:02:31,195 --> 00:02:32,920
This is your marital home, after all.

46
00:02:33,635 --> 00:02:35,320
I wouldn't dare sleep in your bed.

47
00:02:41,632 --> 00:02:42,633
It's okay.

48
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:46,360
I'll have my own house built in a few months anyway.

49
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:49,240
Mm. Don't worry.

50
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:50,751
That's all for now.

51
00:02:51,435 --> 00:02:53,680
Have a safe trip. Bye-bye.

52
00:04:51,931 --> 00:04:54,532
I'm so glad we were born as sisters.

53
00:04:55,568 --> 00:04:56,569
I'm sorry

54
00:04:56,934 --> 00:04:59,640
I couldn't make our dream come true.

55
00:05:00,235 --> 00:05:01,560
In our next life,

56
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,280
I promise I'll make it happen.

57
00:05:04,891 --> 00:05:06,640
I hope you'll be happy.

58
00:05:07,459 --> 00:05:09,160
Live your life for both of us.

59
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:11,440
Don't tell anyone about this.

60
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,960
Don't try to find out the truth.

61
00:05:14,552 --> 00:05:16,110
It was all my fault.

62
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:20,221
Please let me go quietly and in peace.

63
00:05:20,859 --> 00:05:21,860
Goodbye.

64
00:06:59,414 --> 00:07:01,360
Ta has loved nature since she was little.

65
00:07:02,838 --> 00:07:04,300
She always wanted a house near the mountains.

66
00:07:05,616 --> 00:07:07,840
I bought this plot of land as a gift for her.

67
00:07:09,952 --> 00:07:11,800
We were going to build twin houses and live side by side.

68
00:07:13,894 --> 00:07:15,360
But Ta never got the chance to live in hers.

69
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:22,920
Why do you think Ta went all the way into the woods to die?

70
00:07:25,758 --> 00:07:27,559
Maybe she didn't want to die in my house.

71
00:07:29,216 --> 00:07:31,880
She wouldn't even sleep upstairs when I offered.

72
00:07:32,411 --> 00:07:34,120
She said it was my marital home.

73
00:07:36,246 --> 00:07:37,920
She was waiting for her own house to be built.

74
00:07:39,483 --> 00:07:41,000
She'd already contacted a contractor.

75
00:07:41,568 --> 00:07:43,850
Construction was supposed to start in just a few months.

76
00:07:46,774 --> 00:07:49,320
She was probably hoping to start a happy family with Jenphop,

77
00:07:49,544 --> 00:07:52,678
with the three of them together.

78
00:07:53,998 --> 00:07:56,014
But who would've thought Jenphop

79
00:07:56,227 --> 00:07:58,520
was planning to kill both her and her baby?

80
00:08:03,331 --> 00:08:05,840
I don't think Jenphop actually meant to kill Ta.

81
00:08:07,768 --> 00:08:09,240
When I came back,

82
00:08:09,579 --> 00:08:12,500
he didn't seem surprised at all to see Ta was still alive.

83
00:08:13,302 --> 00:08:16,144
He actually seemed happy that Ta was back.

84
00:08:16,854 --> 00:08:18,360
He seemed really fond of her.

85
00:08:19,055 --> 00:08:20,056
Almost as if

86
00:08:20,395 --> 00:08:22,560
he wanted to keep her as his plaything for a long time.

87
00:08:24,123 --> 00:08:26,080
He probably only wanted Ta to miscarry,

88
00:08:27,467 --> 00:08:28,880
but the medication was too strong.

89
00:08:31,336 --> 00:08:33,635
Do you think Nopnapha was involved in this?

90
00:08:34,691 --> 00:08:35,692
I'm not sure.

91
00:08:36,430 --> 00:08:39,880
I don't know if Jenphop did it because he was afraid his wife would find out,

92
00:08:40,431 --> 00:08:42,880
or because she already knew and ordered him to do it.

93
00:08:48,766 --> 00:08:49,767
Ta.

94
00:08:51,606 --> 00:08:52,720
Don't worry.

95
00:08:54,646 --> 00:08:56,960
I'll make sure those two pay for what they've done.

96
00:08:58,827 --> 00:09:00,840
They destroyed the family we dreamed of having.

97
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:04,640
I'll destroy their dream family myself.

98
00:09:15,635 --> 00:09:17,136
Couldn't they find anyone else?

99
00:09:17,374 --> 00:09:19,800
Why not get some young women to walk the runway?
They'd look much better than me.

100
00:09:20,707 --> 00:09:23,120
An event of this magnitude deserves a minister, ma'am.

101
00:09:23,672 --> 00:09:25,840
Of all the ministers across the 20 ministries,

102
00:09:26,174 --> 00:09:28,250
you're the only one with such beauty and elegance.

103
00:09:28,744 --> 00:09:30,760
You're the perfect choice for the runway.

104
00:09:31,939 --> 00:09:34,312
Who says? The event organizers?

105
00:09:34,968 --> 00:09:36,069
That's my personal opinion.

106
00:09:36,664 --> 00:09:37,720
I agree, ma'am.

107
00:09:38,638 --> 00:09:40,720
Oh, stop flattering me!

108
00:09:41,096 --> 00:09:43,064
But what if I trip on the runway?

109
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:44,755
I'd embarrass myself in front of the whole world!

110
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:49,040
I've never been afraid to give a political speech,

111
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:51,881
but walking in a fashion show, and alongside Phop, no less.

112
00:09:51,891 --> 00:09:52,892
Oh my!

113
00:09:52,899 --> 00:09:54,536
I think it would be great for your public image, ma'am.

114
00:09:54,910 --> 00:09:57,920
A female minister and her husband modeling traditional Thai outfits

115
00:09:58,718 --> 00:10:00,446
would definitely go viral worldwide.

116
00:10:01,710 --> 00:10:02,711
Well,

117
00:10:04,286 --> 00:10:05,886
if the photos turn out well,

118
00:10:06,387 --> 00:10:08,800
we could use them in the next election campaign, too.

119
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:12,101
- Oshi.
- Yes, ma'am?

120
00:10:12,286 --> 00:10:14,568
Contact a runway coach for me.

121
00:10:14,648 --> 00:10:16,168
Book me an intensive course.

122
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,760
And make an appointment for Phop, too.

123
00:10:18,126 --> 00:10:19,127
Of course, ma'am.

124
00:10:20,571 --> 00:10:24,400
You'll look so elegant and dignified, ma'am.

125
00:10:24,472 --> 00:10:25,473
Absolutely stunning!

126
00:10:30,019 --> 00:10:31,080
A fashion show?

127
00:10:31,707 --> 00:10:34,758
I wish I could go watch. You'd look so handsome, Director.

128
00:10:37,355 --> 00:10:39,000
I'm always handsome.

129
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,880
But I have to walk alongside that power-hungry old hag.

130
00:10:43,288 --> 00:10:44,560
If I had a choice,

131
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:47,960
I'd much rather walk with you.

132
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,201
That would be a dream come true.

133
00:10:51,784 --> 00:10:55,680
Then why don't you put some broken glass in her shoes?

134
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:57,040
That way, I could take her place.

135
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:00,840
You'd go that far?

136
00:11:01,744 --> 00:11:02,760
I'm just kidding.

137
00:11:03,045 --> 00:11:04,520
But it would be nice if you actually did it.

138
00:11:08,299 --> 00:11:09,440
You're a naughty one, aren't you?

139
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:12,301
So naughty!

140
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,001
Ta.

141
00:11:33,483 --> 00:11:34,484
Hey,

142
00:11:36,048 --> 00:11:37,449
whose house have you brought me to?

143
00:11:38,347 --> 00:11:39,348
It's beautiful.

144
00:11:41,462 --> 00:11:43,840
And look at this million-dollar view!

145
00:11:44,864 --> 00:11:45,880
Surprise!

146
00:11:47,072 --> 00:11:48,400
This is our house, Director.

147
00:11:52,070 --> 00:11:53,071
You're kidding.

148
00:11:53,606 --> 00:11:55,200
How could you possibly afford a house like this?

149
00:11:55,910 --> 00:11:58,918
I'm still helping you pay off your student loan.

150
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:04,160
Last year, I found out that a distant relative had passed away.

151
00:12:04,915 --> 00:12:06,483
They owned this land.

152
00:12:06,696 --> 00:12:08,120
They didn't have any children or other heirs.

153
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:12,480
The lawyer tracked me down and found that I was the sole heir to the entire estate.

154
00:12:14,739 --> 00:12:16,360
As for the money to build the house,

155
00:12:17,096 --> 00:12:18,720
I used the money you gave me that I'd saved up.

156
00:12:19,619 --> 00:12:20,620
Director,

157
00:12:22,030 --> 00:12:23,400
this is our home.

158
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:29,401
Really?

159
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:30,901
Yes.

160
00:12:49,051 --> 00:12:50,907
What do you think? Would you like to live here?

161
00:12:52,790 --> 00:12:54,700
This will be where we sit and watch TV.

162
00:12:55,142 --> 00:12:57,670
And over there is our dining table.

163
00:13:03,958 --> 00:13:06,120
But don't you think that dining table looks a little odd?

164
00:13:07,142 --> 00:13:08,143
Not at all.

165
00:13:08,523 --> 00:13:11,524
It's just the right size for the two of us.

166
00:13:12,243 --> 00:13:15,160
Even with a child, it wouldn't be too big or too small.

167
00:13:16,131 --> 00:13:17,320
Shall we go see the bedroom?

168
00:13:19,688 --> 00:13:20,689
Let's go.

169
00:13:27,075 --> 00:13:30,240
A man doesn't need much in life.

170
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:34,253
Good wine, a beautiful atmosphere,

171
00:13:35,966 --> 00:13:37,640
and a woman he feels comfortable with.

172
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,800
That's all it takes to feel like heaven.

173
00:13:43,323 --> 00:13:44,600
But you have a choice, Director.

174
00:13:45,483 --> 00:13:49,104
Just leave that hell behind and come live here in heaven with me.

175
00:13:55,419 --> 00:13:56,840
It's not that simple, Ta.

176
00:13:57,678 --> 00:13:59,679
You know I have a career to think about.

177
00:14:02,096 --> 00:14:03,184
I'd rather call you Phop

178
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,360
than Director.

179
00:14:06,358 --> 00:14:08,854
You said it yourself that all a man needs

180
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:12,240
is good wine, a lovely atmosphere,

181
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:14,321
and a woman who understands him.

182
00:14:17,382 --> 00:14:19,480
You have everything you need right here.

183
00:14:21,046 --> 00:14:24,080
You wouldn't have to beg your wife for promotions

184
00:14:25,411 --> 00:14:27,600
or put up with her constantly pushing you around.

185
00:14:29,806 --> 00:14:30,807
Phop.

186
00:14:32,403 --> 00:14:35,750
Why do you need those fancy insignia on your shoulders

187
00:14:36,342 --> 00:14:38,240
when you have me right here?

188
00:15:05,672 --> 00:15:08,720
Let's be a loving husband and wife for a day, Phop.

189
00:15:09,896 --> 00:15:12,607
Aren't we always like that, darling?

190
00:15:14,886 --> 00:15:17,366
Hello, Minister Nopnapha.

191
00:15:17,579 --> 00:15:19,400
- Hello, Director Jenphop.
- Hello.

192
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:21,120
Hello, Aunt Shane.

193
00:15:21,334 --> 00:15:23,240
Oh, it's been ages since we last saw each other, hasn't it?

194
00:15:23,579 --> 00:15:24,580
Yes.

195
00:15:24,785 --> 00:15:28,320
Not since I organized your appointment celebration.

196
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:31,238
You've been so busy, we haven't had a chance to meet.

197
00:15:31,771 --> 00:15:34,720
When you become Prime Minister,

198
00:15:34,772 --> 00:15:37,240
I'll throw you a grand celebration lasting seven days and nights.

199
00:15:38,126 --> 00:15:39,320
Sounds wonderful!

200
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:43,320
And you're offering to do it for free, right?

201
00:15:43,795 --> 00:15:47,760
Oh, how could I possibly charge the Prime Minister?

202
00:15:48,195 --> 00:15:50,560
But I'd like to organize next year's Olympics in Thailand.

203
00:15:51,310 --> 00:15:52,400
Please leave that to me.

204
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,441
Consider it yours.

205
00:15:56,510 --> 00:15:57,511
Excuse me.

206
00:15:57,891 --> 00:15:59,982
What exactly are we here for?

207
00:16:00,926 --> 00:16:02,536
Oh, look at us, getting carried away chatting.

208
00:16:02,927 --> 00:16:05,360
Let's go rehearse your positions onstage. This way, please.

209
00:16:06,038 --> 00:16:07,440
Is everything ready inside?

210
00:16:08,096 --> 00:16:10,800
Minister Nopnapha is about to rehearse her positions.

211
00:16:11,097 --> 00:16:13,360
When all the lights in the hall go out,

212
00:16:13,478 --> 00:16:15,720
you two will stand right on these marks.

213
00:16:15,779 --> 00:16:17,320
Then strike a beautiful pose.

214
00:16:17,630 --> 00:16:19,700
- Let's give it a try.
- Please, go ahead.

215
00:16:20,275 --> 00:16:21,400
And what happens next?

216
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:25,240
Now imagine the entire hall is completely dark.

217
00:16:25,414 --> 00:16:27,720
Then the music starts on cue.

218
00:16:27,968 --> 00:16:30,155
Hold your poses for a moment.

219
00:16:30,169 --> 00:16:31,680
And suddenly, the lights come on!

220
00:16:31,830 --> 00:16:33,031
Just like that!

221
00:16:34,198 --> 00:16:35,355
So that means

222
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:38,920
I can pick my nose in the dark without anyone seeing, right?

223
00:16:40,598 --> 00:16:41,680
Something like that.

224
00:16:41,824 --> 00:16:43,440
This isn't the time for jokes, Phop.

225
00:16:44,976 --> 00:16:45,977
Please continue, Aunt Shane.

226
00:16:46,182 --> 00:16:48,040
Once the lights come on,

227
00:16:48,083 --> 00:16:50,059
count to three in your head.

228
00:16:50,256 --> 00:16:52,358
One, two, three.

229
00:16:53,734 --> 00:16:56,520
Then follow me over here.

230
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:00,760
Then stop right on this mark.

231
00:17:00,886 --> 00:17:02,667
But remember to smile when you walk.

232
00:17:02,779 --> 00:17:04,283
Pose to the left.

233
00:17:05,270 --> 00:17:07,080
Now pose to the right.

234
00:17:07,552 --> 00:17:09,153
Then walk back.

235
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,120
And link arms, please.

236
00:17:11,456 --> 00:17:13,920
I'm so jealous! Couple of the year!

237
00:17:14,171 --> 00:17:15,840
You two must be so in love.

238
00:17:17,088 --> 00:17:18,651
Head back to that mark, ma'am.

239
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:19,961
Right here, please.

240
00:17:20,801 --> 00:17:23,142
How was that, ma'am? Are you okay?

241
00:17:38,395 --> 00:17:39,640
I've got some intel.

242
00:17:39,824 --> 00:17:42,320
Ta and the Director have built a house in Khao Yai.

243
00:17:42,358 --> 00:17:44,160
They're planning to run away and live together.

244
00:17:48,579 --> 00:17:50,160
Let me touch up your makeup, ma'am.

245
00:17:54,735 --> 00:17:56,520
Hey, can you check on her face?

246
00:17:57,171 --> 00:17:59,240
There is something wrong with her eyes, I guess.

247
00:18:00,126 --> 00:18:02,280
Is something irritating your skin, ma'am?

248
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,960
No, thank you.

249
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,040
Last Saturday,

250
00:18:17,704 --> 00:18:18,705
where did you go?

251
00:18:20,075 --> 00:18:21,076
I had some business to take care of.

252
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:28,880
When did you two build a house together?

253
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:33,000
Who the hell is your informant, huh?

254
00:18:33,939 --> 00:18:35,720
Were they hiding under Ta's car or something?

255
00:18:36,179 --> 00:18:37,360
Don't change the subject!

256
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:40,121
Answer me!

257
00:18:40,235 --> 00:18:42,136
You're planning to move in with her, aren't you?

258
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:43,301
Are you crazy?

259
00:18:43,355 --> 00:18:44,720
- Sit down!
- Answer me! Wait a second.

260
00:18:44,756 --> 00:18:46,120
Excuse me.

261
00:18:46,699 --> 00:18:48,200
Ladies and gentlemen,

262
00:18:48,427 --> 00:18:50,960
We'll go to the standby area.

263
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,960
Follow me, please.

264
00:19:13,312 --> 00:19:15,680
The show begins in five...

265
00:19:16,313 --> 00:19:17,314
Four...

266
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:18,501
Three...

267
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,701
Two...

268
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,360
Please take your marks.

269
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:29,480
So you're moving in with her, aren't you?

270
00:19:29,598 --> 00:19:32,920
Oh, come on! If you're going to make a scene, pick a better time and place.

271
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:34,221
We'll talk after the show.

272
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,201
Answer me.

273
00:19:36,518 --> 00:19:38,240
- You're going to live with her, aren't you?
- Yes, I am!

274
00:19:38,523 --> 00:19:40,054
And I'm taking Titus with me!

275
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:42,360
So she won't grow up to be a complete lunatic like you!

276
00:19:48,134 --> 00:19:49,135
Oh!

277
00:19:49,392 --> 00:19:50,393
What?

278
00:19:51,083 --> 00:19:52,084
Oh, shit.

279
00:19:57,808 --> 00:19:58,880
The music's started.

280
00:20:09,227 --> 00:20:10,360
Walk! Come on!

281
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:12,701
Start walking!

282
00:21:08,310 --> 00:21:12,400
Wow, people on social media are so quick, Ta.

283
00:21:12,475 --> 00:21:14,160
They managed to capture the whole thing.

284
00:21:14,262 --> 00:21:16,100
The screenshots are already all over social media.

285
00:21:16,734 --> 00:21:19,840
You sent that video to provoke Nopnapha at just the right moment.

286
00:21:20,222 --> 00:21:21,640
It worked even better than expected.

287
00:21:21,774 --> 00:21:25,920
Well, since I pulled off the job so perfectly,

288
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,901
don't I deserve a little reward?

289
00:21:38,899 --> 00:21:40,120
Jicama?

290
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,160
Thank you.

291
00:21:49,435 --> 00:21:51,800
That was just a little bonus. Show me your QR code.

292
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:06,080
Wow! That's way more than Nopnapha pays me!

293
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:08,480
Now you should know

294
00:22:09,152 --> 00:22:10,320
whose side you need to be on.

295
00:22:13,419 --> 00:22:15,979
I've always been on your side, Ta.

296
00:22:24,238 --> 00:22:25,239
Phop!

297
00:22:26,062 --> 00:22:27,063
Phop!

298
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:28,881
Stop!

299
00:22:29,352 --> 00:22:30,353
Phop!

300
00:22:30,798 --> 00:22:31,799
Phop!

301
00:22:32,371 --> 00:22:34,200
- I told you to stop.
- Don't touch me!

302
00:22:38,488 --> 00:22:40,312
If you're going to force me back into that show,

303
00:22:40,707 --> 00:22:44,451
I'll humiliate you just like you humiliated me earlier.

304
00:22:45,086 --> 00:22:46,800
And I'll make it a hundred times worse! Go ahead, try me.

305
00:22:48,344 --> 00:22:49,345
I'm sorry.

306
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:51,436
You can shove your apology!

307
00:22:52,398 --> 00:22:55,600
You slapped me in front of the whole world, and now you're apologizing?

308
00:22:57,100 --> 00:22:58,600
What the fuck is your apology supposed to do?

309
00:23:00,912 --> 00:23:02,520
That's why we need to go back inside

310
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:05,344
and show everyone it was all a misunderstanding.

311
00:23:05,462 --> 00:23:08,163
That we're still on good terms, Phop.

312
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:11,841
I can't fucking believe you!

313
00:23:13,376 --> 00:23:14,520
Even after all this,

314
00:23:15,462 --> 00:23:17,568
all you care about is your precious image!

315
00:23:19,232 --> 00:23:22,203
Go ahead! Go back and explain yourself to the whole world

316
00:23:22,435 --> 00:23:24,507
with your pathetic excuses!

317
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:26,363
I'm not that fucking shameless!

318
00:23:27,201 --> 00:23:28,600
Phop! Phop!

319
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:30,401
Phop!

320
00:23:30,464 --> 00:23:31,465
Phop!

321
00:23:34,134 --> 00:23:35,135
Ma'am.

322
00:23:36,365 --> 00:23:37,480
Are you okay, ma'am?

323
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:41,001
I'm fine.

324
00:23:42,851 --> 00:23:44,552
I was just about to head back inside.

325
00:23:49,198 --> 00:23:50,480
Stay strong, ma'am.

326
00:23:51,523 --> 00:23:53,443
My husband has a mistress, too.

327
00:23:55,370 --> 00:23:59,080
But I dealt with that homewrecker once and for all.

328
00:23:59,824 --> 00:24:02,080
Now she can't get anywhere near my husband.

329
00:24:04,700 --> 00:24:05,880
How did you do it?

330
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:08,360
I locked my husband up at home

331
00:24:09,101 --> 00:24:11,600
and had someone guard him 24 hours a day.

332
00:24:13,707 --> 00:24:15,600
I wish I could do that, too.

333
00:24:56,523 --> 00:24:58,758
I'm very sorry to keep you waiting.

334
00:25:00,163 --> 00:25:04,400
Unfortunately, Mr. Jenphop was held up by an urgent matter.

335
00:25:05,832 --> 00:25:08,320
And he won't be able to join us.

336
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:11,560
We understand.

337
00:25:12,651 --> 00:25:16,395
Take her husband at the most inconvenient times.

338
00:25:18,019 --> 00:25:25,320
We have to learn as women to have dinners and enjoy good food on our own.

339
00:25:25,971 --> 00:25:31,771
Let's say cheers to good good and good women.

340
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:35,081
Cheers!

341
00:25:35,280 --> 00:25:36,281
Cheers!

342
00:25:41,120 --> 00:25:45,120
By now, everyone has probably seen this video that's gone viral worldwide.

343
00:25:45,163 --> 00:25:47,164
The incident took place during a Thai fashion show

344
00:25:47,220 --> 00:25:51,300
at the World Finance and Development Summit, hosted by Thailand this year.

345
00:25:51,521 --> 00:25:55,160
Minister Nopnapha, who was modeling as a guest of honor,

346
00:25:55,259 --> 00:25:59,382
appeared to brush her hand across the face of her husband, Director Jenphop,

347
00:25:59,430 --> 00:26:00,960
who was walking the runway alongside her.

348
00:26:01,126 --> 00:26:04,200
But some viewers believe she actually slapped him.

349
00:26:04,299 --> 00:26:06,760
Foreign media outlets have even mocked the incident,

350
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:10,000
dubbing Thailand the "Land of Slap."

351
00:26:11,198 --> 00:26:13,171
Oh, my God!

352
00:26:14,147 --> 00:26:15,148
It's all over!

353
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:19,100
The reputation she's worked so hard to build is completely ruined!

354
00:26:19,771 --> 00:26:22,360
Mom, what made Aunt Napha so angry that she totally lost it?

355
00:26:22,720 --> 00:26:24,896
What else could it be? There's only one thing.

356
00:26:24,992 --> 00:26:26,907
And this is no laughing matter!

357
00:26:27,193 --> 00:26:31,040
We can't let one wicked woman bring down the whole country!

358
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:33,936
Veekit, you know that woman.

359
00:26:33,984 --> 00:26:35,600
Can't you find a way to deal with her?

360
00:26:38,838 --> 00:26:42,120
Since the footage of the incident was released,

361
00:26:42,220 --> 00:26:45,920
the public has been raising a lot of questions about what happened.

362
00:26:45,960 --> 00:26:47,566
How would you like to explain it, ma'am?

363
00:26:48,195 --> 00:26:50,440
First of all, I'd like to apologize

364
00:26:50,456 --> 00:26:53,400
if my actions have caused any concern.

365
00:26:53,846 --> 00:26:55,320
It was really nothing.

366
00:26:55,400 --> 00:26:59,320
Jenphop was just feeling a little nervous and overwhelmed.

367
00:26:59,401 --> 00:27:00,920
So he asked me to slap him to snap him out of it.

368
00:27:01,296 --> 00:27:04,080
We were in the dark, so I thought no one could see us.

369
00:27:04,100 --> 00:27:06,840
But the lights happened to come on at that exact moment.

370
00:27:06,901 --> 00:27:09,720
That's why the footage has caused this misunderstanding.

371
00:27:09,926 --> 00:27:11,440
And during the fashion show,

372
00:27:11,467 --> 00:27:15,000
we also noticed some pushing and pulling on the runway.

373
00:27:15,068 --> 00:27:16,369
Could you explain what happened there, ma'am?

374
00:27:17,451 --> 00:27:19,720
His legs stiffened up and he couldn't take a step.

375
00:27:19,830 --> 00:27:21,920
So I had to pull him along a little.

376
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:26,440
But Director Jenphop looked very upset throughout the show, ma'am.

377
00:27:26,875 --> 00:27:29,320
He'd been watching videos of international male models.

378
00:27:29,712 --> 00:27:33,600
They all keep straight faces on the catwalk.

379
00:27:33,969 --> 00:27:35,720
He wanted to look cool, so he copied them.

380
00:27:36,300 --> 00:27:37,301
- That's all.
- I see.

381
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:40,640
We apologize. It was our first time modeling.

382
00:27:40,798 --> 00:27:43,120
We'll do better next time.

383
00:27:50,363 --> 00:27:52,952
If your aunt weren't a minister,

384
00:27:53,272 --> 00:27:54,840
she could make a living as a con artist.

385
00:27:55,500 --> 00:27:56,901
She's such a convincing liar.

386
00:27:59,843 --> 00:28:00,844
Not really.

387
00:28:02,814 --> 00:28:03,880
When someone's truly good at lying,

388
00:28:04,900 --> 00:28:06,600
you can't even tell they're lying.

389
00:28:10,200 --> 00:28:11,400
You came all this way so late at night.

390
00:28:11,870 --> 00:28:14,560
Don't tell me you're here to catch me lying again.

391
00:28:15,611 --> 00:28:16,612
No.

392
00:28:17,254 --> 00:28:20,198
I came to ask what you did to Aunt Napha

393
00:28:20,600 --> 00:28:21,801
that made her completely lose it like that.

394
00:28:23,320 --> 00:28:24,921
Why don't you wait and ask her yourself?

395
00:28:25,259 --> 00:28:26,520
She'll be home soon, won't she?

396
00:28:28,363 --> 00:28:29,720
I want to hear it from you.

397
00:28:31,590 --> 00:28:33,250
I want to see your face when you answer.

398
00:28:38,896 --> 00:28:40,960
I want to know if you have a heart at all.

399
00:28:47,534 --> 00:28:48,535
Listen.

400
00:28:49,411 --> 00:28:52,883
Of everyone involved, Nopnapha is the most heartless.

401
00:28:53,500 --> 00:28:54,840
Jenphop comes in second.

402
00:28:56,470 --> 00:28:58,600
I had too much heart.

403
00:28:59,467 --> 00:29:01,880
So much that I became a victim of both your aunt and uncle.

404
00:29:03,558 --> 00:29:05,040
Ta, things have gone too far now.

405
00:29:06,294 --> 00:29:08,680
Stop speaking in riddles.

406
00:29:09,590 --> 00:29:10,800
Just tell me straight.

407
00:29:11,584 --> 00:29:12,600
Tell me everything.

408
00:29:13,526 --> 00:29:15,920
What the hell is really going on with all this crazy stuff you're doing?

409
00:29:30,520 --> 00:29:32,680
Why don't you go ask your beloved aunt and uncle?

410
00:29:33,598 --> 00:29:35,720
You live under the same roof as the two people behind all this,

411
00:29:36,638 --> 00:29:38,300
yet you come all the way here to ask me?

412
00:29:50,974 --> 00:29:52,300
You're hiding something from me.

413
00:29:53,900 --> 00:29:54,901
Yes.

414
00:29:56,624 --> 00:29:59,000
Go on, see if you can figure out what it is.

415
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:01,520
You've been suspicious of me for so long.

416
00:30:02,939 --> 00:30:06,440
When are you finally going to figure it out? I'm dying to tell you!

417
00:30:14,494 --> 00:30:15,760
You're not Mutta, are you?

418
00:30:21,376 --> 00:30:22,377
I've had that feeling

419
00:30:23,867 --> 00:30:26,120
ever since you came back after disappearing for two weeks.

420
00:30:29,734 --> 00:30:32,680
Tell me who you really are.

421
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:40,881
I am...

422
00:30:48,232 --> 00:30:49,233
Mutta.

423
00:31:55,102 --> 00:31:56,103
Ma'am.

424
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:00,501
That.

425
00:32:14,107 --> 00:32:15,108
Ma'am.

426
00:32:16,500 --> 00:32:17,501
Ma'am.

427
00:33:00,558 --> 00:33:01,559
I'm okay now.

428
00:33:03,331 --> 00:33:04,600
Take me home.

429
00:33:06,147 --> 00:33:07,148
Yes, ma'am.

430
00:33:07,244 --> 00:33:09,440
When you get home, take your medicine and go straight to bed.

431
00:33:09,579 --> 00:33:10,580
Don't look at social media.

432
00:33:11,024 --> 00:33:12,838
I'll pick you up at seven tomorrow morning.

433
00:33:15,472 --> 00:33:18,800
Isn't the meeting in the afternoon? Why so early?

434
00:33:19,300 --> 00:33:22,080
You said you wanted to go over some technical terms with the interpreter beforehand.

435
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:24,440
Oh, my goodness!

436
00:33:25,080 --> 00:33:26,120
I completely forgot!

437
00:33:27,400 --> 00:33:31,101
Tomorrow's meeting is very important. We can't afford a single mistake.

438
00:33:41,606 --> 00:33:42,607
Who is it?

439
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:45,601
Prime Minister Narong.

440
00:33:53,547 --> 00:33:55,560
I know you're already under a lot of stress.

441
00:33:56,475 --> 00:33:57,476
So

442
00:33:58,443 --> 00:33:59,800
I'm not going to reprimand you any further.

443
00:34:02,582 --> 00:34:04,590
I think you should go home and get some rest today.

444
00:34:04,886 --> 00:34:06,280
As for this afternoon's meeting,

445
00:34:06,950 --> 00:34:08,040
I'll send Wichit in your place.

446
00:34:09,500 --> 00:34:10,920
That wouldn't be appropriate, Prime Minister.

447
00:34:11,501 --> 00:34:15,102
Every other country is sending a minister.

448
00:34:15,948 --> 00:34:19,949
How can we, as the host country, send a deputy minister?

449
00:34:21,019 --> 00:34:24,840
Well, ministers from other countries don't slap their spouses in front of the media!

450
00:34:27,099 --> 00:34:29,400
And if I still allow you to carry out your duties today,

451
00:34:32,672 --> 00:34:36,320
the international community will accuse me of turning a blind eye to domestic violence.

452
00:34:38,731 --> 00:34:40,520
But I've already explained in an interview

453
00:34:40,982 --> 00:34:43,200
that my husband and I weren't fighting.

454
00:34:44,715 --> 00:34:47,317
If I don't attend this afternoon's meeting,

455
00:34:47,611 --> 00:34:50,960
won't that mean everything I said was a lie?

456
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:52,814
That's your problem to deal with.

457
00:34:53,971 --> 00:34:55,480
What I have to deal with

458
00:34:56,067 --> 00:34:58,612
is the Thai government's image in the eyes of the world.

459
00:35:01,080 --> 00:35:02,481
And I know about the slapping incident

460
00:35:03,627 --> 00:35:04,640
at the Ministry, too.

461
00:35:06,165 --> 00:35:07,166
Both incidents, in fact.

462
00:35:09,600 --> 00:35:11,301
But I chose to turn a blind eye.

463
00:35:12,601 --> 00:35:13,602
This time, though,

464
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:16,001
I really can't ignore it anymore.

465
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:20,001
Minister Nopnapha,

466
00:35:20,400 --> 00:35:22,101
I think you should

467
00:35:22,336 --> 00:35:24,624
get your marital problems sorted out first

468
00:35:24,875 --> 00:35:27,000
before coming back to serve the country.

469
00:35:46,611 --> 00:35:49,520
The climate here is perfect for growing grapes.

470
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:53,080
Many Thai wine brands source their grapes from this region.

471
00:35:53,294 --> 00:35:55,520
How many rai should we plant, Phop?

472
00:35:57,920 --> 00:35:59,960
Sweetheart, I'm getting old, you know.

473
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:02,361
I'm not even sure I could plant a single vine!

474
00:36:02,520 --> 00:36:05,040
I don't mean you have to plant them yourself. We'll hire people!

475
00:36:05,998 --> 00:36:08,600
I think we should build a winery near the house.

476
00:36:08,995 --> 00:36:12,160
That way, you can walk over and taste some wine every morning. How does that sound?

477
00:36:13,912 --> 00:36:14,960
Actually, that sounds pretty good.

478
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:18,840
If I get drunk from all that tasting, I can just crawl home!

479
00:36:20,136 --> 00:36:22,960
Then I'll combine the house and the winery into one building.

480
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:24,760
So you can work from home!

481
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:27,560
That's a great idea!

482
00:36:29,238 --> 00:36:32,200
But I doubt we'd have any wine left to sell.

483
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:34,640
I'd drink it all myself!

484
00:36:47,638 --> 00:36:48,639
Napha.

485
00:36:52,624 --> 00:36:53,625
We need to talk.

486
00:37:03,104 --> 00:37:04,120
I remember

487
00:37:08,806 --> 00:37:10,955
I fell in love with you because you were a capable woman.

488
00:37:13,286 --> 00:37:14,448
But after we got married,

489
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:16,841
I realized

490
00:37:17,931 --> 00:37:19,120
that very quality

491
00:37:20,971 --> 00:37:22,640
was what ended up hurting me.

492
00:37:25,488 --> 00:37:27,649
You see me as a henpecked husband,

493
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:31,160
like one in a comic strip you can yell at or hit whenever you please, right?

494
00:37:33,863 --> 00:37:36,040
And you probably thought I'd never leave you

495
00:37:37,165 --> 00:37:39,360
and would always come crawling back to you, didn't you?

496
00:37:45,358 --> 00:37:46,359
Yeah.

497
00:37:47,966 --> 00:37:49,500
Maybe that was true before.

498
00:37:53,763 --> 00:37:55,080
But not anymore.

499
00:38:00,230 --> 00:38:02,240
And I know I've caused you a lot of pain, too.

500
00:38:06,102 --> 00:38:08,241
Let's stop making each other miserable, Napha.

501
00:38:11,472 --> 00:38:12,480
Let's get a divorce.

502
00:38:38,278 --> 00:38:39,279
Are you asleep?

503
00:38:39,883 --> 00:38:41,440
Dad asked Mom for a divorce.

504
00:38:47,907 --> 00:38:50,360
I'm so sad. Can we have a voice call?

505
00:38:50,451 --> 00:38:51,680
I need someone to talk to.

506
00:39:09,915 --> 00:39:10,916
Hello?

507
00:39:13,656 --> 00:39:15,600
How are you holding up, Wonyoung?

508
00:39:16,286 --> 00:39:17,800
I don't even know how to feel.

509
00:39:18,691 --> 00:39:19,840
It feels like my whole world is falling apart.

510
00:39:21,288 --> 00:39:23,000
I used to wish they'd get divorced.

511
00:39:23,891 --> 00:39:26,840
But now that it's actually happening, I feel awful.

512
00:39:27,710 --> 00:39:28,920
Try to stay calm.

513
00:39:29,736 --> 00:39:31,120
Are they really getting divorced?

514
00:39:32,160 --> 00:39:33,579
Dad asked Mom for a divorce,

515
00:39:34,006 --> 00:39:35,080
but she hasn't given him an answer yet.

516
00:39:35,926 --> 00:39:38,520
She's been through so much today. She's probably still in shock.

517
00:39:39,184 --> 00:39:40,864
I feel so fucking bad for my mom.

518
00:39:41,824 --> 00:39:43,227
But I feel sorry for myself, too.

519
00:39:44,320 --> 00:39:46,921
Why does that bitch have to mess up our family like this?

520
00:39:47,520 --> 00:39:48,840
Why can't she go ruin someone else's life?

521
00:39:49,781 --> 00:39:51,640
I'm sorry on behalf of that mistress.

522
00:39:53,462 --> 00:39:55,080
Maybe she has her reasons.

523
00:39:56,240 --> 00:39:57,760
Why are you apologizing for her?

524
00:39:58,198 --> 00:39:59,800
You're supposed to be cursing her out with me!

525
00:40:01,126 --> 00:40:02,127
Yeah.

526
00:40:03,248 --> 00:40:04,700
Being a mistress is definitely wrong.

527
00:40:06,486 --> 00:40:08,000
But there are two sides to every story.

528
00:40:09,496 --> 00:40:11,022
What if your dad lied to her?

529
00:40:11,900 --> 00:40:12,901
No way!

530
00:40:13,219 --> 00:40:14,440
I've met that bitch before.

531
00:40:14,990 --> 00:40:16,707
She doesn't look that stupid.

532
00:40:17,251 --> 00:40:18,840
She's probably just pretending to be.

533
00:40:20,720 --> 00:40:22,921
Wonyoung, I have to go to bed now.

534
00:40:24,011 --> 00:40:26,566
Whatever happens, stay strong, okay?

535
00:40:27,430 --> 00:40:28,720
You can message me anytime.

536
00:40:29,966 --> 00:40:32,627
Okay. Thanks for keeping me company.

537
00:40:33,008 --> 00:40:34,009
Good night.

538
00:40:34,900 --> 00:40:36,360
Good night.

539
00:40:49,123 --> 00:40:52,200
Wow, that plot of land is beautiful.

540
00:40:52,328 --> 00:40:54,400
Where is it? Veekit, you should take me there sometime.

541
00:40:54,429 --> 00:40:55,430
Mom.

542
00:40:57,800 --> 00:40:58,920
Oh, my God!

543
00:40:59,500 --> 00:41:01,880
That woman really is shameless!

544
00:41:02,672 --> 00:41:05,254
Going on a trip with someone else's husband like it's nothing!

545
00:41:07,238 --> 00:41:08,280
They weren't on a trip.

546
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:11,200
That land belongs to Mutta.

547
00:41:12,088 --> 00:41:14,520
And that house is hers, too. It was just built.

548
00:41:15,600 --> 00:41:16,601
What?

549
00:41:17,500 --> 00:41:20,360
If she owns a house by the mountains, she can't be poor.

550
00:41:22,115 --> 00:41:24,000
I heard she inherited some money.

551
00:41:25,246 --> 00:41:26,936
And she has another lump sum, too.

552
00:41:27,891 --> 00:41:29,200
Good heavens!

553
00:41:30,112 --> 00:41:32,320
From a whore to a wealthy woman.

554
00:41:33,723 --> 00:41:35,259
But it's strange, isn't it?

555
00:41:35,574 --> 00:41:37,542
If she's got that much money,

556
00:41:37,803 --> 00:41:40,400
why is she still leeching off Jenphop?

557
00:41:40,850 --> 00:41:43,080
Or does she really love Phop?

558
00:41:43,851 --> 00:41:44,852
Mom.

559
00:41:50,120 --> 00:41:51,400
Aunt Napha, try not to stress yourself out.

560
00:41:52,563 --> 00:41:54,200
Could you send me that video?

561
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:56,201
I want to check something.

562
00:42:28,155 --> 00:42:29,840
Come on, Ta. Get in the car.

563
00:42:30,847 --> 00:42:31,848
Where are we going?

564
00:42:33,102 --> 00:42:34,520
Away from here.

565
00:42:56,752 --> 00:42:57,753
Hey, everyone!

566
00:42:58,736 --> 00:43:00,680
Does anyone have a friend at the Land Department?

567
00:43:02,867 --> 00:43:04,760
I've already told Nopnapha I want a divorce.

568
00:43:05,011 --> 00:43:06,760
- I'm just waiting for her to set a date to sign the papers.
- [Chiang Mai]

569
00:43:07,200 --> 00:43:09,086
I can't face anyone today.

570
00:43:09,560 --> 00:43:11,400
Stay here with me and get away from it all for a while, Ta.

571
00:43:11,832 --> 00:43:13,300
Let's call it a practice honeymoon.

572
00:43:14,483 --> 00:43:16,440
If you're in Chiang Mai, you have to come here, Ta.

573
00:43:16,755 --> 00:43:18,200
Wat Phra That Doi Suthep.

574
00:43:29,099 --> 00:43:30,811
Okay, thank you.

575
00:43:33,000 --> 00:43:36,195
The airline confirmed that Mr. Jenphop and that Mutta

576
00:43:36,323 --> 00:43:37,880
flew to Chiang Mai, ma'am.

577
00:43:40,880 --> 00:43:43,560
Since I've been suspended from my duties anyway,

578
00:43:44,515 --> 00:43:47,200
Might as well make the most of my time off by slapping that mistress around!

579
00:44:05,518 --> 00:44:08,240
Do you know how many steps there are here?

580
00:44:13,291 --> 00:44:14,520
306 steps.

581
00:44:15,136 --> 00:44:16,320
You've done your homework!

582
00:44:17,552 --> 00:44:19,120
Now, which step do you want to die on?

583
00:44:19,371 --> 00:44:20,372
Take your pick.

584
00:44:34,016 --> 00:44:37,760
I swear before this sacred pagoda that I will marry Mutta.

585
00:44:38,160 --> 00:44:39,499
And I'll love her and her alone.

586
00:44:39,942 --> 00:44:43,480
I swear I'll love you until the day I die.

587
00:44:43,595 --> 00:44:45,520
And if either of us breaks this vow,

588
00:44:45,931 --> 00:44:47,384
may they be damned.

589
00:44:47,622 --> 00:44:51,120
May they suffer worse than hell on earth.

590
00:44:52,176 --> 00:44:53,360
Do you have any rooms available?

591
00:44:53,414 --> 00:44:54,520
We're fully booked.

592
00:44:57,371 --> 00:44:59,728
Are you really willing to sleep with me after your uncle?

593
00:45:01,915 --> 00:45:03,160
Why don't you let me prove it?

594
00:45:06,451 --> 00:45:07,452
Nina.
